# 低频词汇 List04
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List04核心词汇

decree /dɪˈkriː/ n./v. 法令；颁布 The president issued a decree banning protests. 总统颁布了禁止抗议的法令。
dedicate /ˈdedɪkeɪt/ v. 奉献 He dedicated his life to scientific research. 他将一生奉献给了科学研究。
defect /ˈdiːfekt/ n./v. 缺陷；叛逃 The product was recalled due to a defect. 产品因缺陷被召回。
defy /dɪˈfaɪ/ v. 违抗 She defied expectations and won the competition. 她打破预期赢得了比赛。
delegate /ˈdelɪɡeɪt/ v./n. 委派；代表 The manager delegated the task to her team. 经理将任务委派给了她的团队。
denounce /dɪˈnaʊns/ v. 谴责 The organization denounced human rights violations. 该组织谴责了侵犯人权的行为。
depict /dɪˈpɪkt/ v. 描绘 The novel depicts life in rural China. 这部小说描绘了中国农村的生活。
deplete /dɪˈpliːt/ v. 耗尽 Natural resources are being rapidly depleted. 自然资源正在迅速枯竭。
deploy /dɪˈplɔɪ/ v. 部署 The military deployed troops along the border. 军队沿边境部署了部队。
deprecate /ˈdeprɪkeɪt/ v. 反对；贬低 He deprecated the use of violence. 他反对使用暴力。
designate /ˈdezɪɡneɪt/ v. 指定 The area was designated as a nature reserve. 该地区被指定为自然保护区。
desolate /ˈdesələt/ adj. 荒凉的 The landscape was desolate and barren. 景观荒凉而贫瘠。
despatch /dɪˈspætʃ/ v./n. 派遣 The company despatched the goods immediately. 公司立即发运了货物。
detach /dɪˈtætʃ/ v. 分离 He tried to detach his personal feelings from the decision. 他试图将个人感情与决定分开。
deviate /ˈdiːvieɪt/ v. 偏离 The results deviate significantly from the norm. 结果显著偏离了常态。
devise /dɪˈvaɪz/ v. 设计；发明 The team devised a clever solution. 团队设计了一个巧妙的解决方案。
dignity /ˈdɪɡnəti/ n. 尊严 Everyone deserves to be treated with dignity. 每个人都应该被有尊严地对待。
dilemma /dɪˈlemə/ n. 两难境地 The ethical dilemma has no easy answer. 这个道德困境没有简单的答案。
dilute /daɪˈluːt/ v./adj. 稀释 The company diluted its brand by expanding too fast. 公司因扩张过快而稀释了品牌。
discern /dɪˈsɜːn/ v. 辨别 It is hard to discern the truth in this situation. 在这种情况下很难辨别真相。
discourse /ˈdɪskɔːs/ n. 论述；话语 Academic discourse requires precise language. 学术论述需要精确的语言。
disperse /dɪˈspɜːs/ v. 分散 The crowd dispersed after the rally. 集会后人群散去了。
disposition /ˌdɪspəˈzɪʃn/ n. 性情；处置 She has a cheerful disposition. 她性情开朗。
dissolve /dɪˈzɒlv/ v. 溶解；解散 Parliament was dissolved ahead of the election. 议会在选举前被解散了。
distort /dɪˈstɔːt/ v. 歪曲 The media can distort the facts. 媒体可能会歪曲事实。
doctrine /ˈdɒktrɪn/ n. 主义；教义 The doctrine of free trade has been widely debated. 自由贸易学说已被广泛讨论。
domain /dəˈmeɪn/ n. 领域 This topic falls within the domain of psychology. 这个话题属于心理学领域。
dominion /dəˈmɪniən/ n. 统治权；领土 The king exercised dominion over the land. 国王对这片土地行使统治权。
doom /duːm/ n./v. 厄运；注定 The project was doomed to fail from the start. 这个项目从一开始就注定要失败。
dose /dəʊs/ n./v. 剂量 The doctor prescribed a low dose of the medication. 医生开了低剂量的药物。
